# Every path below decides who may sign off a listing, what counts as verified
# evidence, how that evidence is shown, what CI and the deploy run, or the written
# policy behind them. A change to any of them needs an approving review from an
# organisation owner. The `main-protection` ruleset
# requires code-owner review, and approval from someone other than the last person
# to push, so an owner's own change here needs the other owner's approval.
#
# GitHub reads this file from the pull request's base branch, so a pull request
# cannot change who has to review it. Owners must keep write access to the
# repository: GitHub silently ignores a code owner without it.
#
# The last matching pattern wins. Every line names the same owners, so order does
# not change anything today; the more specific lines come last so they stay
# owner-only if a broader line is ever widened.

